. UI Layer (Frontend)
The UI uses a custom JavaScript file (e.g., gis-picker-integration.js) to integrate the Google Drive Picker and Google Identity Services (GIS).
When the user clicks the "Import from Google Drive" button:
The GIS OAuth flow is triggered to authenticate the user and obtain a Google access token.
The Google Drive Picker API is launched, allowing the user to select a file (usually a Google Sheet).
Once a file is picked, the Picker returns a fileId and fileName.
Yes, the Google Drive Picker API is used on the UI side.

2. UI → Backend Communication
The UI sends a POST request to the backend endpoint /bulk-upload-service/bulk-upload/importFromGoogleDrive.
The request body contains:
fileId (from Picker)
fileName (from Picker)
The request includes a user header (serialized user info, typically set by the gateway or UI).
3. Backend Controller
BulkUploadController#importFromGoogleDrive receives the request.
It:
Deserializes the user header.
Validates fileId (must not be null/empty).
Calls the service layer: bulkUploadService.importFromGoogleDrive(fileId, fileName, user).
4. Backend Service
BulkUploadServiceImpl#importFromGoogleDrive:
Validates fileId.
Calls googleSheetsClient.readRows(fileId, user) to fetch rows from the selected Google Sheet.
Maps the rows to DataSourceCriteria objects.
Calls bulkUploadDao.bulkSarfUpdate(criteria) to update the database.
If successful, queues a Locus API call for further processing.
5. Summary
Picker API is used in the UI to let the user select a file from Google Drive.
The backend does not interact with the Picker API directly; it receives the fileId and processes the file via Google Sheets API.
The flow is:
UI (Picker + GIS) → Backend Controller → Service → DAO/Database
